Package: kmod-keys-encrypted
Version: 6.12.37-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.12.37~a846d1ca01313b709a943855e9e9197a-r1), kmod-crypto-cbc, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-rng, kmod-crypto-sha256, kmod-keys-trusted
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1750714327
Architecture: aarch64_generic
Installed-Size: 40960
Filename: kmod-keys-encrypted_6.12.37-r1_aarch64_generic.ipk
Size: 10156
SHA256sum: 932380ee3c3679b5830253fb44f4b8d3da32a51cecf2788946dee8ffad39dcab
Description:  This module provides support for create/encrypting/decrypting keys
 in the kernel.  Encrypted keys are kernel generated random numbers,
 which are encrypted/decrypted with a 'master' symmetric key. The
 'master' key can be either a trusted-key or user-key type.
 Userspace only ever sees/stores encrypted blobs.

Package: kmod-keys-trusted
Version: 6.12.37-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.12.37~a846d1ca01313b709a943855e9e9197a-r1), kmod-crypto-hash, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-sha1, kmod-tpm
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1750714327
Architecture: aarch64_generic
Installed-Size: 20480
Filename: kmod-keys-trusted_6.12.37-r1_aarch64_generic.ipk
Size: 4707
SHA256sum: 48c9bea6807ceaa58a3692c511be02e8f831e989b61d53c17708c194a64559c0
Description:  This module provides support for creating, sealing, and unsealing
 keys in the kernel. Trusted keys are random number symmetric keys,
 generated and RSA-sealed by the TPM. The TPM only unseals the keys,
 if the boot PCRs and other criteria match.  Userspace will only ever
 see encrypted blobs.

